---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const tools = [
  { name: "Pen & Marker", icon: "pen", text: "Sketch a thought or highlight the detail you want someone to notice." },
  { name: "Line & Arrow", icon: "arrow", text: "Point to a control or connect the parts of your explanation." },
  { name: "Rectangle & Ellipse", icon: "ellipse", text: "Frame an area or circle the problem." },
  { name: "Text", icon: "text", text: "Add a note directly on the screenshot with a transparent background." },
  { name: "Blur Marker & Pixelate", icon: "pixelate", text: "Visually obscure an area. These effects are not a secure-redaction guarantee." },
  { name: "Select", icon: "select", text: "Move, resize, or edit an individual annotation object." },
];
const questions = [
  { question: "Is AniShot available to download?", answer: "A verified public download is not available yet. A free Mac App Store release is planned. AniShot is currently in development." },
  { question: "Can I annotate during a call without saving?", answer: "You can draw on a frozen screen and dismiss the overlay without exporting. Check that participants can see AniShot in the selected sharing mode. Meeting compatibility is still being verified." },
  { question: "Does AniShot upload screenshots?", answer: "The current app processes screenshots and annotations locally and has no screenshot-upload service or account requirement. Clipboard syncing, saved-file syncing, and meeting sharing depend on other software and your settings." },
  { question: "Can AniShot record my screen?", answer: "Screen recording is not implemented. AniShot currently exports PNG screenshots." },
  { question: "Which Macs can use AniShot?", answer: "Public release requirements are not finalized. The current development build is for Apple silicon. It declares macOS 14 as its minimum, but minimum-OS acceptance and distribution checks remain pending. Intel support has not been established." },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="AniShot Screen Capture for Mac | Aniloom Technologies" description="Freeze your screen before selecting an area. Annotate with drawing tools, then copy or save a PNG. AniShot is in development; a free Mac App Store release is planned.">
  <main id="main-content" class="anishot">
    <section class="anishot-hero section-shell" aria-labelledby="anishot-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Screenshots and annotation for Mac</p>
      <h1 id="anishot-title">AniShot<br />Screen Capture</h1>
      <div class="anishot-hero__lower">
        <div>
          <h2 class="anishot-benchmark" id="capture-benchmark">86 ms <span>average on two displays.<a href="/anishot/capture-timing/" aria-label="Capture timing methodology">*</a></span></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="anishot-hero__copy">
          <p>Freeze your screen before selecting an area. Draw an arrow, highlight a detail, or add a note directly on the frozen image.</p>
          <p>Copy a PNG, save it, or dismiss the overlay when your explanation is done.</p>
          <p class="anishot-availability">In development. A free Mac App Store release is planned.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="#workflow">Explore the capture workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Capture on request</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Freeze first.<br />Select second.</h2></div><p>Activate AniShot with a shortcut or the menu bar icon. It captures the screen before you select an area. Your applications keep running underneath.</p></div>
      <ol class="anishot-steps" role="list">
        <li><span>01</span><h3>Freeze the image.</h3><p>The captured image stays still while you decide what to show. Capture starts when you request it; there is no continuous screen-history buffer.</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><h3>Select the detail.</h3><p>Frame the relevant area on one display, then annotate directly in the same overlay.</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><h3>Make your point.</h3><p>Mark the part that matters. Choose whether to copy, save, or simply close the overlay.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad anishot-reading" aria-labelledby="explain-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">A clear explanation</p>
      <h2 id="explain-title">Draw the point while you explain it.</h2>
      <p>Circle the problem, point to a control, or sketch the next step on the frozen image. You can close the overlay after the explanation without copying or saving a screenshot.</p>
      <p class="anishot-note">During a call, check that your sharing mode includes the AniShot overlay and that participants can see it. AniShot draws on a frozen image; your meeting application handles screen sharing.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Drawing tools</p><h2 id="tools-title">Choose the mark<br />the detail needs.</h2></div><p>Change size and color where the tool supports them. Blur and pixelation use size controls. Separate Tools and Layers panels adapt to the space beside your selection.</p></div>
      <div class="anishot-tools">
        {tools.map((tool) => <article><img src={`/assets/images/anishot/${tool.icon}.png`} width="64" height="64" alt="" loading="lazy" /><div><h3>{tool.name}</h3><p>{tool.text}</p></div></article>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad anishot-reading" aria-labelledby="layers-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Editable annotations</p><h2 id="layers-title">Revise your explanation as you go.</h2>
      <p>Select an annotation on the image or in Layers. Move it, resize it, change its style, or remove it. Drag its tool icon in Layers to change the order. Undo and Redo let you revise earlier edits.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad" aria-labelledby="export-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PNG export</p><h2 id="export-title">Finish the way<br />you need.</h2></div><p>Copy an annotated PNG into a message or document, save it to a folder, or dismiss the overlay without exporting.</p></div>
      <div class="anishot-exports">
        <article><kbd>⌘ C</kbd><h3>Copy</h3><p>Copy a PNG to the macOS clipboard and close the overlay.</p></article>
        <article><kbd>⌘ S</kbd><h3>Save</h3><p>Choose a destination in the native Save dialog. Cancelling or failing to save keeps your session open.</p></article>
        <article><kbd>Esc</kbd><h3>Dismiss</h3><p>Close without exporting. While editing text, the first Escape cancels that edit.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad anishot-reading" aria-labelledby="local-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Local processing</p><h2 id="local-title">Processed on your Mac.</h2>
      <p>AniShot processes screenshots and annotations on your Mac. It captures when you request it and releases the session image when you close the overlay. The current app has no screenshot-upload service or account requirement.</p>
      <p class="anishot-note">Copy puts a PNG on the macOS clipboard. Save writes to the destination you choose. Clipboard syncing, cloud-synced folders, and meeting software follow their own settings.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad anishot-reading" aria-labelledby="settings-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your setup</p><h2 id="settings-title">Set the shortcut and panel size you prefer.</h2>
      <p>Use Shift+Command+9, Shift+Command+4, both, or a custom capture shortcut. Appearance scales Tools, Layers, and the action panel from 50% to 150% without changing drawing widths or exported pixels.</p>
      <p>You can also enable launch at login and choose whether an outside double-click dismisses the overlay.</p>
      <p class="anishot-note">First setup asks for macOS screen access, then your shortcut. System-shortcut takeover requires your confirmation. Another app's reserved shortcut may need to be released in that app's settings.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell section-pad" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Availability and compatibility</p><h2 id="faq-title">Questions before using AniShot.</h2>
      <div class="anishot-faq">{questions.map((item) => <details><summary>{item.question}</summary><p>{item.answer}</p></details>)}</div>
      <aside class="anishot-release" aria-labelledby="release-status-title"><h3 id="release-status-title">Public release verification is pending.</h3><p>The current 0.8.6 build 52 disk image is Apple Development signed, not Developer ID signed or notarized. Its recorded Gatekeeper execution assessment was rejected. It is not offered here as a verified public download.</p></aside>
    </section>

  </main>
  <section class="surface-dark anishot-closing"><div class="section-shell section-pad"><p class="eyebrow">AniShot Screen Capture</p><h2>Make the detail clear.</h2><p>Freeze the screen, annotate the part that matters, and choose whether to copy, save, or simply close it.</p><p class="anishot-availability">In development. A free Mac App Store release is planned.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .anishot-hero { padding-block: clamp(130px, 12vw, 180px) 64px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .anishot-hero h1 { margin: 24px 0 64px; font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 8vw, 8rem); font-weight: 500; }
  .anishot-hero__lower { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 60px; align-items: start; }
  .anishot-benchmark { margin: 0; color: var(--link); font-size: clamp(3rem, 5.5vw, 5.5rem); font-weight: 500; }
  .anishot-benchmark > span { display: block; margin-top: 12px; color: var(--text); font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.7rem); line-height: 1.35; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .anishot-benchmark a { color: var(--link); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .15em; }
  .anishot-hero__copy > p:first-child { color: var(--text); font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .anishot-availability { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  .anishot-steps, .anishot-exports { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .anishot-steps li, .anishot-exports article { padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .anishot-steps li > span { color: var(--link); font-family: "DM Mono", monospace; }
  .anishot h3 { font-size: 1.45rem; font-weight: 500; margin-block: 20px 12px; }
  .anishot-reading { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .anishot-reading h2, .anishot-faq + aside h3 { max-width: 840px; }
  .anishot-reading > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 840px; }
  .anishot-note { padding-left: 22px; border-left: 2px solid var(--line-strong); margin-top: 28px; }
  .anishot-tools { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0 48px; }
  .anishot-tools article { display: flex; align-items: start; gap: 22px; padding-block: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .anishot-tools img { width: 48px; height: 48px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .anishot-tools h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .anishot-tools p { margin-bottom: 0; }
  kbd { display: inline-block; min-width: 72px; padding: 10px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--surface-solid); color: var(--text); font-family: "DM Mono", monospace; }
  .anishot-faq { margin-top: 36px; }
  .anishot-faq details { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 22px 0; }
  .anishot-faq details:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .anishot-faq summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--text); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .anishot-faq p { max-width: 820px; margin: 20px 0 0; }
  .anishot-release { margin-top: 40px; max-width: 840px; padding: 0 0 0 22px; border-left: 2px solid var(--line-strong); }
  .anishot-release h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  #workflow, #capture-benchmark { scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  .anishot-closing h2 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 6rem); font-weight: 500; margin-block: 18px 28px; }
  .anishot-closing p { max-width: 720px; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .anishot-hero h1 { margin-bottom: 38px; }
    .anishot-hero__lower { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .anishot-steps, .anishot-exports, .anishot-tools { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .anishot-steps, .anishot-exports { gap: 18px; }
    .anishot-hero__copy > p:first-child { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  }
</style>
